WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.520
You need one tree that loses its leaves in fall, one you can reach safely and have

2
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:08.520
permission to visit.

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.740
Bring a phone or camera and paper.

4
00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:14.963
Stand 10 to 20 steps back, so the whole tree fits in the photo.

5
00:00:15.403 --> 00:00:19.643
Pick a landmark, and take every photo from there, facing the same way.

6
00:00:20.343 --> 00:00:21.483
Your child predicts first.

7
00:00:22.417 --> 00:00:24.597
Visit about once a month for 15 minutes.

8
00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:26.757
Notice the weather and look for animals.

9
00:00:27.357 --> 00:00:30.397
In much of Virginia, buds swell and open in March and April.

10
00:00:31.037 --> 00:00:32.037
Dates vary.

11
00:00:32.417 --> 00:00:34.857
Stay with your child at the tree on every visit.

12
00:00:35.477 --> 00:00:39.277
Feet stay on the ground, with no climbing, and nothing from the tree goes in a

13
00:00:39.277 --> 00:00:39.517
mouth.
